WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.437
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.387
For each instance that survived the gate,
the audit records its authentication mode,

3
00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:09.387
every usable login by type,
the state of the S A login,

4
00:00:09.387 --> 00:00:11.387
and the account the engine runs as.

5
00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:12.946
Every later step, Arc,

6
00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:17.624
login migration and N T L M
elimination, depends on that record.

7
00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:20.888
And it's re-run after every
change, to measure progress.

8
00:00:20.888 --> 00:00:23.821
In this module you audit
four fictional instances,

9
00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:27.174
rank their findings, and rerun
the audit thirty days later.

10
00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:30.500
Runbook R oh three is
read-only from start to finish.
